@*
    A map question as it is answered: the world, and beneath it a bar naming whatever the last tap
    hit, with the control that locks it in.

    The bar is not decoration. A world map on a phone with no pan and no zoom is a picture in which
    Belgium and the Netherlands are two neighbouring thumbprints; without something saying which one
    the tap landed on, the player only finds out at the reveal. Tapping again moves the pick, so the
    bar is a chance to correct rather than a receipt.

    The same component is #77's authoring control, where an admin sets a question's target by
    clicking the map. That is why the confirm button is optional and the tolerance radius is a
    parameter: an author needs to see the circle their radius actually draws, and has no "lock it
    in" step at all — they have a form.
*@
@inject WorldMapAsset Asset
@inject Translator L

<WorldMap Shape="Shape" BaseLayer="BaseLayer" Disabled="Disabled" ToleranceKm="ToleranceKm"
          Selection="Selection" SelectionChanged="SelectionChanged" Label="@Label" />

<div class="mapbar @(Selection is null ? "mapbar--empty" : null)" role="status">
    @if (Selection is null)
    {
        <span class="grow">@L[Shape == 1 ? "map.tapPoint" : "map.tapCountry"]</span>
    }
    else if (Selection.IsCountry)
    {
        <span class="mapbar__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="mapbar__name grow" dir="ltr">@MapText.CountryName(_countries, Selection.CountryCode)</span>
        <span class="chip">@Selection.CountryCode</span>
    }
    else
    {
        <span class="mapbar__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="mapbar__coords grow" dir="ltr">@L.Num(MapText.Coordinates(Selection))</span>
    }

    @if (OnConfirm.HasDelegate)
    {
        <button class="btn btn--sm" disabled="@(Selection is null || Disabled)" @onclick="OnConfirm">@L["play.lockIn"]</button>
    }
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>A <c>MapTargetKind</c> ordinal off the card: 0 country, 1 city.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int Shape { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A <c>MapBaseLayer</c> ordinal off the card: 0 blank, 1 borders.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int BaseLayer { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public MapPick? Selection { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public EventCallback<MapPick> SelectionChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Set only where the radius is actually known — #77's admin form. No reveal contract
    /// carries it, so a played round leaves it null and draws no circle.</summary>
    [Parameter] public double? ToleranceKm { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The answer is locked, or the clock has run out.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Disabled { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Supplied by a play screen, where an answer has to be committed; omitted by the admin
    /// form, where the surrounding form is what commits it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnConfirm { get; set; }

    private IReadOnlyList<MapCountry> _countries = [];

    private string Label => L["map.label"];

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync() => _countries = await Asset.LoadAsync();
}
